#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Patch TaskTrove InferredBugs tasks with a verified build and a warning-based verifier (single script).

Everything the pipeline needs lives here: the recipe table (one verified build recipe
per task, exported from the compile audit) is embedded at the end of this file as
EMBEDDED_RECIPES, and artifacts that no longer exist on Maven Central / NuGet.org come
from the public vendor dataset (DEFAULT_VENDOR_URL) or a local --vendor-dir.

Resolution order for every task (each step ends with the same proof: the fixed file must
compile, and a deliberately corrupted target file must fail with a compiler error on
its first line; no recipe is trusted because of where it came from):

  1. the task's row in the recipe table;
  2. every recipe that verified another task of the same project, plus deterministic
     variants (test-compile for test sources, module retargeting through the root
     reactor, lint/descriptor-plugin skips, direct compiler goals, other JDK images);
  3. the try-and-repair loop with a coding agent (``--repair-backend claude|deepseek``),
     which compiles inside a per-task sandbox container and returns a recipe;
  4. otherwise the task row is left unchanged and reported with a warning.

Packaging ships, per task: a Dockerfile based on one of eight shared images, the repository
snapshot on which the warning was reproduced with the buggy file, ``setup_files/build_setup.sh``
(the recipe's setup step, when any) and ``setup_files/build.sh`` (its build step), the
analyzer's install script, a verifier, and any vendored artifacts. The verifier replays
setup+build on a fresh snapshot with the submitted file under the task's pinned Infer or
InferSharp release and rewards a file that compiles, no longer has the task's warning and has
no warning that neither the buggy file nor the reference has (see README.md). Tasks whose
warning the audit could not reproduce and see removed are left out (DISCARDED_TASKS).

Example:
  python data/patchers/patch.py --input tasks.parquet \\
    --output repaired/tasks.parquet --cache-dir /mnt/.../inferredbugs_patch_cache \\
    --matches matches.jsonl --repositories repositories_v5.jsonl \\
    --recipes data/patchers/inferredbugs_recipes.jsonl --cached-only --limit 3 --verify-package

``--print-prompts`` prints the repair-loop prompts. ``--repair-backend none`` (default)
drops unresolved tasks with a warning instead of calling any model.
"""
